      "answer_text": "To convert the base 7 number $530_7$ to a decimal (base 10) value, we use the positional notation formula:\n\n$$\\text{Value} = (d_n \\times 7^n) + \\dots + (d_1 \\times 7^1) + (d_0 \\times 7^0)$$\n\nFor the digits $5, 3, 0$:\n1. The digit $0$ is in the $7^0$ place: $0 \\times 7^0 = 0 \\times 1 = 0$\n2. The digit $3$ is in the $7^1$ place: $3 \\times 7^1 = 3 \\times 7 = 21$\n3. The digit $5$ is in the $7^2$ place: $5 \\times 7^2 = 5 \\times 49 = 245$\n\nNow, sum the values:\n$$245 + 21 + 0 = 266$$\n\n266",
